                <pb facs="0627" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.48B/505: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-10-22T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                                1924—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>172. Your 247, September 29, noon.</p>
                <p>Red Cross has deposited with the Department $466,140.88 for which you may draw a
                    draft the proceeds of which you may turn over to the appropriate Japanese
                    authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
